            <div xml:id="d37">

                <pb facs="0100" n="26" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg26"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/561</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Denmark</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Egan</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-17T12:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 17, 1917, noon</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received 6.35 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>591. Germany offering higher and higher bids for peace to Russia. Cadet Party
                    which has seized the revolutionary movement <pb facs="0101" n="27" xml:id="pg27"
                    /> unable to hold out against workingmen’s association. If the United States
                    could give Russia some tangible evidence that it is really in the war such as a
                    technical corps sent to Russia from the United States or the announcement of
                    some special assistance the separate peace proposals might be nullified. Foreign
                    Minister here believes that peace in July is possible; he is influenced by
                    socialistic opinion. Baron Buxhöveden, Russian Minister
                    here, has been dismissed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Egan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
